  "source_manifest_entries_verified": 25,
  "published_description": "Computational evidence for Growth-law and model consistency in driven ion-acoustic turbulence , by Taylor Kalin. Software version 1.0.0. This package supplies original mathematical consistency controls for Liu and colleagues’ complete arXiv:2309.05563v2 and current Journal of Plasma Physics article, DOI 10.1017/S0022377824000060 , read together with its acknowledgement-only erratum. The audit distinguishes displayed growth, threshold, force, dielectric and beta expressions from actual implemented formulas. It preserves the alternative Gaussian convention and positive source normalizations. Declared released-input and historical-source semantics are documented, including conservative self-collisions and fixed spatial source forcing. Conditional Poisson source-energy controls are not measured source power or a refutation of nonlinear simulation results. The immutable computational commit is 65f92f1fc9c9419a1240fb9a7c658bb1303aae72 ; the distinct tested Git tree is 109f70e8192bf1a8bf244b0ca84353e7cd42edf1. All 50 files are frozen; the artifact manifest records the other 49 members without self-reference. The archive is 392,029 bytes, SHA-256 b1d6cb3074bfa050a3d66ced16685bd1991f7a867b5b1ad5e4214487f9c02c4a, MD5 3e80b5c302c6a26cc911ce199e7e70fa. The original producer runs with Python’s standard library. Three numerical outputs match between Python 3.12.14 and 3.13.7. NumPy 2.3.5 and Matplotlib 3.11.2 generate two explanatory figures; separate high-precision checks use mpmath 1.3.0. Independent programs are not imported by the producer. No original plasma simulation was run. The package includes independently checked source provenance and the thirteen article-linked MIT input-deposit files with their exact upstream copyright notice. It excludes the manuscript PDF, third-party article PDFs, complete historical solver modules, credentials and original raw simulation outputs. Original code is MIT licensed; original audit text and figures are CC BY 4.0. Third-party inputs retain their upstream MIT terms; the historical solver is not relicensed or redistributed. Taylor Kalin self-funded the work. AI systems assisted source comparison, mathematical checking, programming and drafting. Internal checks are not external human peer review. This is a software record, not manuscript acceptance or a new nonlinear plasma model.",
  "published_source_url": "https://github.com/Teylersf/ion-acoustic-turbulence-consistency-audit/tree/65f92f1fc9c9419a1240fb9a7c658bb1303aae72",
